-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ז/1 (13.12.2016): תשלום קצובת נסיעה לעובדי הוראה
-- The travel allowance after the public-transport reform: the Accountant
-- General's instructions of 11.7.2016 on reimbursing public-transport travel
-- apply to teaching staff from 1.1.2016; the instructions sent to the
-- employers are attached (and not in the corpus — see the hand-off); a
-- retroactive deduction of overpayments follows the Wage Protection Law.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ז/1 — קצובת נסיעה לעובדי הוראה`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p15 The letterhead, the date (13.12.2016), the reference number, the addressee, the greeting and the subject line; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p1 The background: the public-transport reform in force from 1.1.2016, fares cut by 14.5% from February 2016 and the reform extended to every locality in April 2016; no rule of its own.

DECLARE `travel action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the travel allowance by the attached instructions` HAS `travel allowance paid` IS A NUMBER
    `deduct an overpayment retroactively` HAS `overpayment deducted` IS A NUMBER

-- ¶17–¶18: the circular publishes the Accountant General's instructions of
-- 11.7.2016 on reimbursing public-transport travel and how travel is paid to
-- teaching staff from 1.1.2016; it applies from 1.1.2016.
@ref akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3
`the day the circular applies from` MEANS Date 1 1 2016

GIVEN `the month` IS A DATE @desc the first day of the salary month
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the new travel rules apply to` `the month` IF
    `the month` AT LEAST `the day the circular applies from`

-- ¶19: the instructions sent to the employers are attached; act by them.
-- They are not in the corpus, so the allowance they set is an input; the
-- circular sets no deadline of its own.
@ref akn:hc_1/p4
GIVEN `the allowance the attached instructions set` IS A NUMBER @desc the month's travel allowance under the Accountant General's instructions attached to the circular; not in the corpus
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel action`
DECIDE `paying travel by the attached instructions` `the allowance the attached instructions set` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the travel allowance by the attached instructions` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` EQUALS `the allowance the attached instructions set`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "circular 2016-17/1: act by the attached instructions on travel reimbursement"

-- ¶20: a retroactive deduction of an overpayment must follow the Wage
-- Protection Law (whose limits are not restated here: an input). The
-- employer may not deduct beyond what that law allows; no time limit.
@ref akn:hc_1/p5
GIVEN `the deduction the Wage Protection Law allows` IS A NUMBER @desc the most the Wage Protection Law allows to be deducted; an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel action`
DECIDE `deducting an overpayment by the Wage Protection Law` `the deduction the Wage Protection Law allows` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `deduct an overpayment retroactively` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` GREATER THAN `the deduction the Wage Protection Law allows`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "circular 2016-17/1: a retroactive deduction of an overpayment follows the Wage Protection Law"

-- akn:conclusions The signatures (Sonia Peretz) and the list of copies; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

#ASSERT `the new travel rules apply to` (Date 1 2 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `the new travel rules apply to` (Date 1 12 2015)

#TRACE `paying travel by the attached instructions` 300 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the travel allowance by the attached instructions` 300 AT 30
#TRACE `deducting an overpayment by the Wage Protection Law` 100 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct an overpayment retroactively` 100 AT 10
#TRACE `deducting an overpayment by the Wage Protection Law` 100 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct an overpayment retroactively` 150 AT 10

§§ `Property checks`

-- ¶17-¶18 over the first of every month from January 2015 to December
-- 2017: the new rules apply exactly from January 2016, and once they apply
-- they apply to every later month.
`the months checked` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN y YIELD map (GIVEN m YIELD Date 1 m y) (range 1 12)) (LIST 2015, 2016, 2017))
#ASSERT count `the months checked` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD `the new travel rules apply to` d EQUALS (d AT LEAST Date 1 1 2016)) `the months checked`
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN d YIELD `the new travel rules apply to` d) `the months checked`) EQUALS 24
